var documenterSearchIndex = {"docs":
[{"category":"section","location":"#PlanetPostStats","page":"Home","text":"Documentation for PlanetPostStats.\n\n","title":"PlanetPostStats"},{"category":"module","location":"#PlanetPostStats.PlanetPostStats","page":"Home","text":"PlanetPostStats\n\nStatistical post-processing of output from the GISS post-processing program scaleacc, which converts the accumulation (acc) files of NASA GISS ModelE and ROCKE-3D simulations into monthly NetCDF files (e.g. the aij, aijl, taijl products).\n\nThe package is organized into submodules, one per post-processing task. Each submodule receives all simulation- and user-specific information (paths, run identifiers, variables, calendars, seasons, time windows, metadata) as function arguments, so that no source code has to be edited when the post-processing is applied to a different set of simulations or by a different user.\n\nSubmodules\n\nTimeSeriesMeSd: extraction of monthly, seasonal, and annual time series of gridded (ij), zonal-mean (zm), and global-mean (gm) fields from a set of simulations, and calculation of multi-year means and standard deviations of annual means, seasonal means, and the individual months of the annual cycle within a selectable time window. All results are written to NetCDF files.\n\nFurther submodules for other post-processing tasks are meant to be added as src/<SubmoduleName>/<SubmoduleName>.jl and included below.\n\nExample\n\nusing PlanetPostStats\nusing PlanetPostStats.TimeSeriesMeSd\n\ncfg = TimeSeriesConfig(;\n    simpath=\"/path/to/simulations\",\n    runs=[\"MarsDustRun1\"],\n    groups=[InputGroup(\"aij\", [InputVariable(\"prsurf\"; units=\"hPa\")])],\n    sim_period=(YearMonth(1, 1), YearMonth(20, 12)),\n    stat_period=(YearMonth(3, 1), YearMonth(20, 12)),\n    calendar=MARS_CALENDAR,\n    seasons=MARS_SEASONS,\n    output_dir=\"Prsurf\",\n    output_name=\"prsurf\",\n)\nresults = run_timeseries_statistics(cfg)\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PlanetPostStats.PlanetPostStats"},{"category":"module","location":"#PlanetPostStats.TimeSeriesMeSd","page":"Home","text":"TimeSeriesMeSd\n\nSubmodule of PlanetPostStats that turns monthly scaleacc output of one or more ModelE/ROCKE-3D simulations into\n\nmonthly mean time series (mts),\nannual mean time series (ats) of full calendar years,\nseasonal mean time series (sts), one series per season,\nmulti-year means and standard deviations of the annual means (moa, soa),\nmulti-year means and standard deviations of the seasonal means (mos, sos),\nmulti-year means and standard deviations of every month of the annual cycle (mom, som),\n\neach of them for three spatial representations:\n\nij  — the gridded field (longitude × latitude [× level]),\nzm  — the area-weighted zonal mean (latitude [× level]),\ngm  — the area-weighted global mean ([level]).\n\nTwo-dimensional (lon × lat) and three-dimensional (lon × lat × level) variables can be mixed; they are written into the same files. Files containing at least one 3D variable get the representation tags ijl, zml, gml (e.g. *.ijl.mts.nc), files with only 2D variables get ij, zm, gm.\n\nOptionally (PressureLevels), 3D variables are interpolated from the hybrid σ–pressure model layers to pressure levels (linear in ln p, missing below the surface), either into additional files with the tags ijp, zmp, gmp or in place of the model-level fields.\n\nWorkflow\n\nAll settings that may differ between simulations or users are collected in a TimeSeriesConfig. The single entry point run_timeseries_statistics then processes every run listed in the configuration one run at a time (bounded memory), and returns a vector of RunResults containing the paths of the written files and small summary tables of global means for interactive inspection.\n\nTreatment of missing data\n\nAll statistics are computed with PlanetTools.PlanetStatistics (see the adapters in statistics.jl), so the definitions are those of PlanetTools. Missing data are NaN32. One validity threshold threshold (percent, TimeSeriesConfig.threshold, default 80) applies to every step:\n\nzonal means: equal-weight mean over the valid longitudes, valid if at least threshold % of the longitudes are valid (availability = valid fraction);\nglobal means: area-weighted, valid if at least threshold % of the area is valid (availability = valid area fraction);\nannual and seasonal means: month weights (month length, see weight_seasons) times the availability of the input month; valid if at least threshold % of the months of the period are valid (availability = fraction of valid months);\nmulti-year statistics (moa/soa, mos/sos, mom/som): availability-weighted mean and sample standard deviation (Σw(x − μ)² / (V₁ − V₂/V₁), i.e. n − 1 for equal weights), weights = availabilities of the annual/seasonal means (or of the monthly zonal/global means); valid if at least threshold % of the samples are valid; the standard deviation needs at least two valid samples.\n\nOutput files are written with PlanetTools.ReadWritePlanet.writenetcdf. Invalid results are NaN32 in memory and the fill value (TimeSeriesConfig.fill_value, default -1f30) in the output files, with a matching _FillValue attribute.\n\nExample\n\nusing PlanetPostStats.TimeSeriesMeSd\n\ncfg = TimeSeriesConfig(;\n    simpath=\"/path/to/simulations\",\n    runs=[\"MarsDustRun1\"],\n    groups=[\n        InputGroup(\"aij\", [InputVariable(\"prsurf\"; units=\"hPa\")]),\n        InputGroup(\"taijl\", [InputVariable(\"Clay\"; scale=1e-8, units=\"kg kg-1\")]),\n    ],\n    sim_period=(YearMonth(1, 1), YearMonth(20, 12)),\n    stat_period=(YearMonth(3, 1), YearMonth(20, 12)),\n    calendar=MARS_CALENDAR,\n    seasons=MARS_SEASONS,\n    output_dir=\"Tracermass3d\",\n    output_name=\"tracermass3d\",\n)\nresults = run_timeseries_statistics(cfg)\nannual_summary(results)\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PlanetPostStats.TimeSeriesMeSd"},{"category":"constant","location":"#PlanetPostStats.TimeSeriesMeSd.ALL_PRODUCTS","page":"Home","text":"ALL_PRODUCTS\n\nTuple of all output products of run_timeseries_statistics:\n\nsymbol content subdirectory\n:mts monthly mean time series MonthlyTs\n:ats annual mean time series (full calendar years) AnnualTs\n:sts seasonal mean time series (one file per season) SeasonalTs\n:moa multi-year mean and standard deviation of annual means AnnualMeSd\n:mos multi-year mean and standard deviation of seasonal means SeasonalMeSd\n:mom multi-year mean and standard deviation of each month MonthlyMeSd\n\n:moa, :mos, :mom each produce two files per representation, a mean (moa, mos, mom) and a standard deviation file (soa, sos, som).\n\nExample\n\njulia> :mos in ALL_PRODUCTS\ntrue\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PlanetPostStats.TimeSeriesMeSd.ALL_PRODUCTS"},{"category":"constant","location":"#PlanetPostStats.TimeSeriesMeSd.ATTRIBUTES_TO_KEEP","page":"Home","text":"ATTRIBUTES_TO_KEEP\n\nInput variable attributes copied to the output, besides units and long_name, if present. Encoding attributes (scale_factor, add_offset, _FillValue, missing_value) are deliberately not copied: the input is decoded when read, and the output gets its own _FillValue.\n\nExample\n\njulia> \"standard_name\" in ATTRIBUTES_TO_KEEP\ntrue\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PlanetPostStats.TimeSeriesMeSd.ATTRIBUTES_TO_KEEP"},{"category":"constant","location":"#PlanetPostStats.TimeSeriesMeSd.DEFAULT_PRESSURE_LEVELS","page":"Home","text":"DEFAULT_PRESSURE_LEVELS\n\nDefault output pressure levels (hPa) by planet, used by PressureLevels when no levels are given. The key is the lower-case planet name, i.e. the lower-case name of the PlanetCalendar of the configuration (\"mars\" for MARS_CALENDAR). Further planets can be added with DEFAULT_PRESSURE_LEVELS[\"<planet>\"] = [...].\n\n\"mars\": 43 levels from 18.789 hPa to 0.099 hPa, approximately equidistant in ln p (ratio ≈ 0.88 between neighboring levels).\n\nExample\n\njulia> lev = DEFAULT_PRESSURE_LEVELS[\"mars\"];\n\njulia> length(lev), first(lev), last(lev)\n(43, 18.789, 0.099)\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PlanetPostStats.TimeSeriesMeSd.DEFAULT_PRESSURE_LEVELS"},{"category":"constant","location":"#PlanetPostStats.TimeSeriesMeSd.EARTH_NOLEAP_CALENDAR","page":"Home","text":"EARTH_NOLEAP_CALENDAR\n\nPlanetCalendar of ModelE for Earth: 365-day year without leap years (months of 31, 28, 31, 30, 31, 30, 31, 31, 30, 31, 30, 31 days) and a day of 86400 seconds.\n\nExample\n\njulia> days_in_year(EARTH_NOLEAP_CALENDAR)\n365.0\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PlanetPostStats.TimeSeriesMeSd.EARTH_NOLEAP_CALENDAR"},{"category":"constant","location":"#PlanetPostStats.TimeSeriesMeSd.EARTH_SEASONS","page":"Home","text":"EARTH_SEASONS\n\nStandard meteorological seasons for Earth: DJF, MAM, JJA, SON.\n\nExample\n\njulia> [s.name for s in EARTH_SEASONS]\n4-element Vector{String}:\n \"DJF\"\n \"MAM\"\n \"JJA\"\n \"SON\"\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PlanetPostStats.TimeSeriesMeSd.EARTH_SEASONS"},{"category":"constant","location":"#PlanetPostStats.TimeSeriesMeSd.MARS_CALENDAR","page":"Home","text":"MARS_CALENDAR\n\nPlanetCalendar of the ROCKE-3D Mars configuration: 12 months of 61, 66, 66, 65, 60, 54, 50, 47, 46, 47, 51, 56 sols (669 sols per Mars year), and a sol of 88775.245 seconds.\n\nExample\n\njulia> month_weights(MARS_CALENDAR, [YearMonth(1, 2)])\n1-element Vector{Float64}:\n 0.09865470852017937\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PlanetPostStats.TimeSeriesMeSd.MARS_CALENDAR"},{"category":"constant","location":"#PlanetPostStats.TimeSeriesMeSd.MARS_SEASONS","page":"Home","text":"MARS_SEASONS\n\nSeason set for ROCKE-3D Mars: FMA, MJJ, ASO, NDJ (three model months each, starting in February, May, August, November).\n\nExample\n\njulia> [s.first_month for s in MARS_SEASONS]\n4-element Vector{Int64}:\n  2\n  5\n  8\n 11\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PlanetPostStats.TimeSeriesMeSd.MARS_SEASONS"},{"category":"constant","location":"#PlanetPostStats.TimeSeriesMeSd.PRESSURE_INTERPOLATION_NOTE","page":"Home","text":"PRESSURE_INTERPOLATION_NOTE\n\nText of the global attribute Vertical_interpolation of output files with variables on pressure levels.\n\nExample\n\njulia> occursin(\"ln(p)\", PRESSURE_INTERPOLATION_NOTE)\ntrue\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PlanetPostStats.TimeSeriesMeSd.PRESSURE_INTERPOLATION_NOTE"},{"category":"constant","location":"#PlanetPostStats.TimeSeriesMeSd.REP_CELL_METHODS","page":"Home","text":"REP_CELL_METHODS\n\nSpatial part of the cell_methods attribute of the output variables for each spatial representation.\n\nExample\n\njulia> REP_CELL_METHODS[:gm]\n\"; lon, lat: mean\"\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PlanetPostStats.TimeSeriesMeSd.REP_CELL_METHODS"},{"category":"constant","location":"#PlanetPostStats.TimeSeriesMeSd.TIME_LIKE_DIMS","page":"Home","text":"TIME_LIKE_DIMS\n\nDimension names treated as a (singleton) time dimension in input variables and dropped when reading. scaleacc monthly files normally have no time dimension; this makes the reader robust against files that carry a time dimension of length one.\n\nExample\n\njulia> \"time\" in TIME_LIKE_DIMS\ntrue\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PlanetPostStats.TimeSeriesMeSd.TIME_LIKE_DIMS"},{"category":"type","location":"#PlanetPostStats.TimeSeriesMeSd.DerivedVariable","page":"Home","text":"DerivedVariable(name, sources, combine; units, long_name, to_pressure=true)\n\nA variable computed from already loaded variables (input or earlier derived variables) after reading, e.g. the accumulated dust mass mixing ratio over several size bins.\n\ncombine is called as combine(a₁, a₂, …) with the arrays of the variables named in sources (in that order; Float32, dimensions lon × lat [× level] × time, missing values NaN32) and must return an array of the same size. Derived variables are evaluated in the order of TimeSeriesConfig.derived, so a derived variable may use previously derived ones. All sources must have the same dimensionality.\n\nTwo helper constructors for combine are provided: sum_of and, for a whole chain of accumulated sums, cumulative_sums.\n\nArguments\n\nname::AbstractString: output variable name (must be unique).\nsources::AbstractVector{<:AbstractString}: names of the variables combined.\ncombine: function of length(sources) arrays.\n\nKeyword arguments\n\nunits::AbstractString = \"\": units of the result; empty → units of the first source.\nlong_name::AbstractString = name: descriptive name.\nto_pressure::Bool = true: for a 3D result, whether it is interpolated to pressure levels when TimeSeriesConfig.pressure_levels is set (see InputVariable).\n\nExample\n\njulia> d = DerivedVariable(\"ClaySilt1\", [\"Clay\", \"Silt1\"], sum_of(); units=\"kg kg-1\",\n                           long_name=\"Dust mass mixing ratio, clay + silt bin 1\");\n\njulia> d.combine(fill(1f0, 2, 2), fill(2f0, 2, 2))\n2×2 Matrix{Float32}:\n 3.0  3.0\n 3.0  3.0\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PlanetPostStats.TimeSeriesMeSd.DerivedVariable"},{"category":"type","location":"#PlanetPostStats.TimeSeriesMeSd.GridInfo","page":"Home","text":"GridInfo\n\nHorizontal and vertical grid of a run, read from the first available input files.\n\nFields\n\nlon::Vector{Float32}, lat::Vector{Float32}: cell-center coordinates (degrees).\nlevel::Union{Nothing,Vector{Float32}}: layer index coordinate (nothing if no 3D variable is processed).\nplm, ple::Union{Nothing,Vector{Float32}}: reference mid-layer and upper-edge pressures (hPa) of the layers, if present in the input.\nlevel_dimname::String: name of the vertical dimension in the input (e.g. \"level\").\narea::Matrix{Float64}: grid-cell areas (axyp), size (lon, lat).\narea_attrib::OrderedDict{String,Any}: attributes of the area variable.\n\nExample\n\nrd = load_run(cfg, \"RUN1\")\nsize(rd.grid.area) == (length(rd.grid.lon), length(rd.grid.lat))  # true\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PlanetPostStats.TimeSeriesMeSd.GridInfo"},{"category":"type","location":"#PlanetPostStats.TimeSeriesMeSd.InputGroup","page":"Home","text":"InputGroup(product::AbstractString, variables::AbstractVector{InputVariable})\n\nA scaleacc output product (e.g. \"aij\", \"aijl\", \"taijl\") and the variables to be read from its monthly files. One monthly file per product is expected for every month of the simulation period; the file name is constructed by TimeSeriesConfig.filename (default scaleacc_filename).\n\nVariables may be two-dimensional (lon × lat) or three-dimensional (lon × lat × level); the dimensionality is detected from the first available file.\n\nExample\n\njulia> g = InputGroup(\"aijl\", [InputVariable(\"z\"; units=\"m\"), InputVariable(\"airmass\")]);\n\njulia> [v.name for v in g.variables]\n2-element Vector{String}:\n \"z\"\n \"airmass\"\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PlanetPostStats.TimeSeriesMeSd.InputGroup"},{"category":"type","location":"#PlanetPostStats.TimeSeriesMeSd.InputVariable","page":"Home","text":"InputVariable(name; scale=1.0, units=\"\", long_name=\"\", to_pressure=true)\n\nA variable to be read from a scaleacc output product (see InputGroup).\n\nscaleacc stores many quantities in scaled units, given in the units attribute (e.g. tracer mixing ratios in units of 1e-8 kg kg⁻¹). After reading, values are multiplied by scale, so that the internal and the output data are in the units units; values and units attribute of the output files are consistent.\n\nAny scale_factor/add_offset/_FillValue/missing_value attributes of the input file are applied by NCDatasets when reading (CF decoding) before scale is applied.\n\nArguments\n\nname::AbstractString: variable name in the scaleacc file (e.g. \"prsurf\").\n\nKeyword arguments\n\nscale::Real = 1.0: multiplicative factor converting file values to units.\nunits::AbstractString = \"\": units after scaling; empty → taken from the file's units attribute (only sensible if scale == 1).\nlong_name::AbstractString = \"\": descriptive name; empty → the file's long_name.\nto_pressure::Bool = true: for a 3D variable, whether it is interpolated to pressure levels when TimeSeriesConfig.pressure_levels is set (see PressureLevels). Set it to false for quantities that are integrals over a model layer (e.g. the air mass per layer in kg m⁻²), which have no meaning at a pressure level; such variables stay on the model levels. Ignored for 2D variables.\n\nExample\n\njulia> v = InputVariable(\"Clay\"; scale=1e-8, units=\"kg kg-1\");\n\njulia> v.scale, v.to_pressure\n(1.0e-8, true)\n\njulia> InputVariable(\"airmass\"; units=\"kg m-2\", to_pressure=false).to_pressure\nfalse\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PlanetPostStats.TimeSeriesMeSd.InputVariable"},{"category":"type","location":"#PlanetPostStats.TimeSeriesMeSd.OutputEntry","page":"Home","text":"OutputEntry\n\nOne variable as written to one set of output files.\n\nFields\n\nfileset::Symbol: :main (regular files) or :pressure (additional files on pressure levels, PressureLevels(…; mode=:add)).\nname::String: variable name.\nattrib::OrderedDict{String,Any}: output attributes.\nvertical::Symbol: :none (2D), :model (model levels), or :pressure.\ndata::Function: function without arguments returning the monthly field; for pressure levels it performs the interpolation, so that interpolated fields exist only while the variable is processed.\n\nExample\n\nentries = output_entries(cfg, load_run(cfg, \"MarsDustRun1\"))\n[(e.fileset, e.name, e.vertical) for e in entries]\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PlanetPostStats.TimeSeriesMeSd.OutputEntry"},{"category":"type","location":"#PlanetPostStats.TimeSeriesMeSd.OutputFile","page":"Home","text":"OutputFile\n\nAn output NetCDF file created by create_output_file. Data variables are added with write_field!, which appends to the file with PlanetTools.ReadWritePlanet.writenetcdf.\n\nFields\n\npath::String: file path.\nrep::Symbol: spatial representation (:ij, :zm, or :gm).\ntime_cell_method::String: temporal part of cell_methods (e.g. \"time: annual mean\").\nhas_time::Bool: whether variables get a time dimension.\nlevel_dimname::String: name of the vertical dimension.\n\nExample\n\nof = create_output_file(\"x.nc\", cfg, rd, :gm, true; time_cell_method=\"time: monthly mean\",\n                        time_months=rd.months)\nwrite_field!(of, cfg, \"z\", gm_of_z, rd.variables[\"z\"].attrib, :model)\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PlanetPostStats.TimeSeriesMeSd.OutputFile"},{"category":"type","location":"#PlanetPostStats.TimeSeriesMeSd.Period","page":"Home","text":"Period\n\nAn averaging period in a monthly record: first is the first month (label), slots the indices of all months of the period in the monthly record (consecutive, ascending).\n\nExample\n\njulia> p = Period(YearMonth(1, 1), 1:12);\n\njulia> length(p.slots)\n12\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PlanetPostStats.TimeSeriesMeSd.Period"},{"category":"type","location":"#PlanetPostStats.TimeSeriesMeSd.PeriodMeans","page":"Home","text":"PeriodMeans\n\nTemporal means over periods (years or occurrences of one season) of the gridded field and of its zonal and global means, with availability weights (fraction of valid months of the period; 0 where the threshold is not met). Returned by annual_means and seasonal_means.\n\nFields\n\nij, ij_w: (Lon, Lat, [Lev], Period).\nzm, zm_w: (1, Lat, [Lev], Period).\ngm, gm_w: (1, 1, [Lev], Period).\n\nExample\n\nan = annual_means(x, sm, months, w; threshold=80)\nsize(an.gm, ndims(an.gm))     # number of years\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PlanetPostStats.TimeSeriesMeSd.PeriodMeans"},{"category":"type","location":"#PlanetPostStats.TimeSeriesMeSd.PlanetCalendar","page":"Home","text":"PlanetCalendar(name, days_in_month; day_length=\"\", month_names=DEFAULT_MONTH_NAMES)\n\nModel calendar of a planet: the lengths of the 12 model months and descriptive metadata.\n\nThe month lengths are used as weights when monthly means are averaged into seasonal and annual means: month m gets the weight days_in_month[m] / days_in_year(calendar). The unit of days_in_month is irrelevant for the weights (only ratios enter), but by convention it is the number of local solar days (sols on Mars).\n\nArguments\n\nname::AbstractString: planet or calendar name, written to the output metadata.\ndays_in_month: 12 month lengths (any real numbers > 0), in local days.\n\nKeyword arguments\n\nday_length::AbstractString = \"\": length of one local day with unit, e.g. \"88775.245 seconds\" for Mars; written as attribute day_length of the time coordinate (omitted when empty).\nmonth_names: 12 three-letter month labels used in output file names.\ncf_calendar::AbstractString = lowercase(name): value of the CF calendar attribute of the time coordinate. A name that is not a CF standard calendar (e.g. \"mars\") declares a user-defined calendar, whose month lengths are written as attribute month_lengths; CF readers then do not convert the time values into Earth dates.\n\nPredefined calendars\n\nMARS_CALENDAR: ROCKE-3D Mars calendar, months of 61, 66, 66, 65, 60, 54, 50, 47, 46, 47, 51, 56 sols (669 sols per year).\nEARTH_NOLEAP_CALENDAR: ModelE 365-day calendar without leap years.\n\nExample\n\njulia> cal = PlanetCalendar(\"TOI-700d\", fill(10.0, 12); day_length=\"864000 seconds\");\n\njulia> days_in_year(cal)\n120.0\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PlanetPostStats.TimeSeriesMeSd.PlanetCalendar"},{"category":"type","location":"#PlanetPostStats.TimeSeriesMeSd.PressureLevels","page":"Home","text":"PressureLevels(levels=nothing; surface_pressure=\"prsurf\", mode=:add)\n\nInterpolation of the 3D variables from the hybrid σ–pressure model layers of ModelE/ROCKE-3D to pressure levels in the output (see interpolate_to_pressure for the method). Set as TimeSeriesConfig.pressure_levels; requires TimeSeriesConfig.vertical (VerticalCoordinate) and the reference mid-layer pressures plm in the input files.\n\nWithout levels (nothing), the default levels of the planet of the configuration are used (default_pressure_levels of TimeSeriesConfig.calendar.name, e.g. the 43 Mars levels of DEFAULT_PRESSURE_LEVELS for MARS_CALENDAR); explicit levels override the default. The levels in use are returned by output_pressure_levels.\n\nThe interpolation is done on the monthly means of each column, using the monthly mean surface pressure of the column, before any temporal or spatial averaging. All products (time series, multi-year statistics; gridded, zonal, and global means) are then computed on the pressure levels. Pressure levels below the local surface are missing, so zonal and global means at high pressures cover only the area above the surface and are subject to TimeSeriesConfig.threshold.\n\nVariables with to_pressure = false (InputVariable, DerivedVariable) and 2D variables are not interpolated.\n\nArguments\n\nlevels = nothing: pressure levels in hPa (the unit of the surface pressure and of plm), any order, positive and unique; written as coordinate plev in the given order. nothing: default levels of the planet.\n\nKeyword arguments\n\nsurface_pressure::AbstractString = \"prsurf\": name of the 2D surface-pressure variable (hPa) among the configured variables.\nmode::Symbol = :add:\n:add — the model-level output is written as without pressure levels, and the interpolated variables are written in addition to separate files with the tags ijp, zmp, gmp;\n:replace — the interpolated variables are written on pressure levels instead of model levels into the regular files; 3D variables with to_pressure = false stay on model levels in the same files.\n\nExample\n\njulia> pl = PressureLevels();                        # planet default\n\njulia> pl.levels === nothing, pl.mode\n(true, :add)\n\njulia> PressureLevels([6.0, 5.0, 4.0, 3.0, 2.0, 1.0, 0.5, 0.1]; mode=:replace).levels[1]\n6.0\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PlanetPostStats.TimeSeriesMeSd.PressureLevels"},{"category":"type","location":"#PlanetPostStats.TimeSeriesMeSd.RunData","page":"Home","text":"RunData\n\nAll input data of one run, as returned by load_run.\n\nFields\n\nrun::String: run identifier.\nmonths::Vector{YearMonth}: monthly record, from the first month of cfg.sim_period to the last month for which at least one input file exists.\ngrid::GridInfo: grid description.\nvariables::OrderedDict{String,VariableData}: input and derived variables, in output order.\navailable::Matrix{Bool}: available[g, t] is true if the file of input group g exists for month t of months.\n\nExample\n\nrd = load_run(cfg, \"RUN1\")\ncollect(keys(rd.variables))\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PlanetPostStats.TimeSeriesMeSd.RunData"},{"category":"type","location":"#PlanetPostStats.TimeSeriesMeSd.RunResult","page":"Home","text":"RunResult\n\nResult of processing one run with run_timeseries_statistics.\n\nFields\n\nrun::String: run identifier.\nmonths::Vector{YearMonth}: monthly record that was processed.\nfiles::Vector{String}: paths of all files written.\nannual::DataFrame: multi-year statistics of the annual global means of all 2D variables, columns Varname, N_years, MOA, SOA, Experiment, for interactive inspection.\nseasonal::DataFrame: same for seasonal global means, columns Varname, Season, N_seasons, MOS, SOS, Experiment.\n\nExample\n\nres = run_timeseries_statistics(cfg)\nfirst(res).annual\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PlanetPostStats.TimeSeriesMeSd.RunResult"},{"category":"type","location":"#PlanetPostStats.TimeSeriesMeSd.SeasonSpec","page":"Home","text":"SeasonSpec(name::AbstractString, first_month::Integer, length::Integer)\n\nA season of length consecutive months starting in month first_month. Seasons may wrap into the following year (e.g. SeasonSpec(\"DJF\", 12, 3)); the season is then labeled with the year of its first month (the year of the December). name is used in output file names, e.g. FMA_0001-0020.<name><run>.ij.sts.nc.\n\nArguments\n\nname: label of the season (e.g. \"JJA\").\nfirst_month: first month, 1 ≤ first_month ≤ 12.\nlength: number of months, 1 ≤ length ≤ 12.\n\nPredefined season sets\n\nEARTH_SEASONS: DJF, MAM, JJA, SON.\nMARS_SEASONS: FMA, MJJ, ASO, NDJ.\n\nExample\n\njulia> s = SeasonSpec(\"NDJ\", 11, 3)\nSeasonSpec(\"NDJ\", 11, 3)\n\njulia> season_months(s)\n3-element Vector{Int64}:\n 11\n 12\n  1\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PlanetPostStats.TimeSeriesMeSd.SeasonSpec"},{"category":"type","location":"#PlanetPostStats.TimeSeriesMeSd.SpatialMeans","page":"Home","text":"SpatialMeans\n\nZonal and global means of a monthly field with their availability weights, as returned by planet_means.\n\nFields\n\nzm, zm_w: zonal mean and fraction of valid longitudes, (1, Lat, [Lev], Time).\ngm, gm_w: area-weighted global mean and valid area fraction, (1, 1, [Lev], Time).\n\nAvailabilities are 0 where the threshold is not met (the mean is then NaN).\n\nExample\n\nsm = planet_means(x, area; threshold=80)\nsize(sm.gm)\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PlanetPostStats.TimeSeriesMeSd.SpatialMeans"},{"category":"type","location":"#PlanetPostStats.TimeSeriesMeSd.TimeAxis","page":"Home","text":"TimeAxis(reference::YearMonth, units::AbstractString)\nTimeAxis(; reference=YearMonth(0, 12), units=\"months since 0000-12\")\n\nDefinition of the numerical time coordinate written to the time-series output files.\n\nThe coordinate value of a period (month, season, or year) is the number of months from reference to the first month of that period, months_between(reference, first). One common unit (months) is therefore used for monthly, seasonal, and annual series. The string units is written verbatim as the units attribute and must describe reference in the convention of the user.\n\nWith the default reference = YearMonth(0, 12), the first month of model year 1 (YearMonth(1, 1)) has the coordinate value 1, so a monthly series starting in January of year 1 has time = 1, 2, …, n.\n\nIn addition, every time-series file contains the integer variables year(time) and month(time) with the first model month of each period, which are unambiguous irrespective of the units string.\n\nExample\n\njulia> ax = TimeAxis(; reference=YearMonth(0, 12), units=\"months since 0023-12-56\");\n\njulia> time_value(ax, YearMonth(2, 1))\n13\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PlanetPostStats.TimeSeriesMeSd.TimeAxis"},{"category":"type","location":"#PlanetPostStats.TimeSeriesMeSd.TimeSeriesConfig","page":"Home","text":"TimeSeriesConfig(; kwargs...)\n\nComplete, user- and simulation-specific configuration of the time-series and statistics post-processing performed by run_timeseries_statistics.\n\nRequired keyword arguments\n\nsimpath::AbstractString: directory containing one subdirectory per run.\nruns::AbstractVector{<:AbstractString}: run identifiers; input files of run r are expected in joinpath(simpath, r, postdir).\ngroups::AbstractVector{InputGroup}: scaleacc products and variables to read.\nsim_period::Tuple{YearMonth,YearMonth}: first and last month of the input files. Runs may end earlier; the record of each run ends with the last month for which at least one input file exists.\nstat_period::Tuple{YearMonth,YearMonth}: window for the multi-year statistics. Only periods (years, seasons) lying entirely inside the window are used.\noutput_dir::AbstractString: name of the output directory created in every run directory (e.g. \"Tracermass3d\").\noutput_name::AbstractString: tag used in output file names (e.g. \"tracermass3d\").\n\nOptional keyword arguments\n\npostdir = \"Post\": subdirectory of a run directory with the scaleacc files.\noutput_root = nothing: if given, output goes to joinpath(output_root, run, output_dir) instead of joinpath(simpath, run, output_dir).\nderived = DerivedVariable[]: variables computed after reading (see DerivedVariable, cumulative_sums).\ncalendar = EARTH_NOLEAP_CALENDAR: PlanetCalendar.\nseasons = EARTH_SEASONS: vector of SeasonSpec.\ntime_axis = TimeAxis(): numerical time coordinate, see TimeAxis.\nvertical = nothing: VerticalCoordinate of the model layers; written as metadata to 3D output and needed for pressure_levels.\npressure_levels = nothing: PressureLevels for the interpolation of the 3D variables to pressure levels; nothing → output on model levels only.\nthreshold = 80.0: validity threshold in percent (see module documentation).\nweight_seasons = true: weight months by their length in seasonal means, as in annual means (on Mars the month lengths range from 46 to 66 sols); false gives equal weights to the months of a season.\nproducts = ALL_PRODUCTS: subset of ALL_PRODUCTS to compute and write.\nfill_value = -1f30: value written for missing data (_FillValue).\narea_variable = \"axyp\": name of the grid-cell area variable in the input files (the output files always call it axyp).\nglobal_attributes = OrderedDict{String,Any}(): global attributes of all output files (the attributes Experiment and File_creation_time are added per file).\nfilename = nothing: function (ym, product, run) -> String giving the input file name; nothing → scaleacc_filename.\ndeflatelevel = 0: NetCDF-4 compression level (0 … 9) of the output variables.\noverwrite = true: overwrite existing output files; if false, an existing file raises an error.\n\nExample\n\ncfg = TimeSeriesConfig(;\n    simpath=\"/path/to/simulations\",\n    runs=[\"MarsDustRun1\"],\n    groups=[InputGroup(\"aij\", [InputVariable(\"prsurf\"; units=\"hPa\")])],\n    sim_period=(YearMonth(1, 1), YearMonth(20, 12)),\n    stat_period=(YearMonth(3, 1), YearMonth(20, 12)),\n    calendar=MARS_CALENDAR,\n    seasons=MARS_SEASONS,\n    output_dir=\"Prsurf\",\n    output_name=\"prsurf\",\n)\nvalidate_config(cfg)\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PlanetPostStats.TimeSeriesMeSd.TimeSeriesConfig"},{"category":"type","location":"#PlanetPostStats.TimeSeriesMeSd.VariableData","page":"Home","text":"VariableData\n\nMonthly record of one variable of one run.\n\nFields\n\ndata::Array{Float32}: values with dimensions (lon, lat, time) for 2D variables or (lon, lat, level, time) for 3D variables; missing values are NaN32.\nattrib::OrderedDict{String,Any}: output attributes (units, long_name, …).\nis3d::Bool: true for variables with a vertical dimension.\n\nExample\n\nv = load_run(cfg, \"RUN1\").variables[\"prsurf\"]\nv.is3d, size(v.data)   # (false, (72, 46, 240))\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PlanetPostStats.TimeSeriesMeSd.VariableData"},{"category":"type","location":"#PlanetPostStats.TimeSeriesMeSd.VerticalCoordinate","page":"Home","text":"VerticalCoordinate(ls1::Integer, psf::Real, ptop::Real)\n\nParameters of the hybrid sigma–pressure vertical coordinate of ModelE/ROCKE-3D, written as scalar metadata variables LS1, Psf, and Ptop to all files containing 3D variables.\n\nBelow layer ls1 the coordinate is σ with σₑ = (pₑ − ptop)/(psf − p_top).\n\nArguments\n\nls1: first layer of pure pressure coordinates above the σ layers.\npsf: global mean surface pressure used for the σ definition (hPa).\nptop: pressure at the bottom of layer ls1 (hPa).\n\nExample\n\njulia> vc = VerticalCoordinate(31, 6.86, 0.2);\n\njulia> vc.ls1\n31\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PlanetPostStats.TimeSeriesMeSd.VerticalCoordinate"},{"category":"type","location":"#PlanetPostStats.TimeSeriesMeSd.YearMonth","page":"Home","text":"YearMonth(year::Integer, month::Integer)\n\nLabel of one model month: model year year (any integer, typically ≥ 1 for ModelE and ROCKE-3D runs) and month month (1 … 12). YearMonths are totally ordered (earlier < later), can be shifted by an integer number of months with +/-, and the number of months between two labels is obtained with months_between.\n\nThe type deliberately carries no information on the length of a month; that is a property of the PlanetCalendar.\n\nArguments\n\nyear::Integer: model year.\nmonth::Integer: month of the year, 1 ≤ month ≤ 12; anything else throws an ArgumentError.\n\nExample\n\njulia> a = YearMonth(3, 11)\nYearMonth(3, 11)\n\njulia> a + 3\nYearMonth(4, 2)\n\njulia> months_between(YearMonth(1, 1), a)\n34\n\njulia> YearMonth(1, 12) < YearMonth(2, 1)\ntrue\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PlanetPostStats.TimeSeriesMeSd.YearMonth"},{"category":"method","location":"#PlanetPostStats.TimeSeriesMeSd.absmonth-Tuple{PlanetPostStats.TimeSeriesMeSd.YearMonth}","page":"Home","text":"absmonth(ym::YearMonth) -> Int\n\nAbsolute month counter 12 * year + month - 1, used for ordering and arithmetic of YearMonth values. Consecutive months have consecutive counters.\n\nExample\n\njulia> absmonth(YearMonth(0, 1)), absmonth(YearMonth(1, 1))\n(0, 12)\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PlanetPostStats.TimeSeriesMeSd.absmonth"},{"category":"method","location":"#PlanetPostStats.TimeSeriesMeSd.alloc_period_means-Tuple{Any, PlanetPostStats.TimeSeriesMeSd.SpatialMeans, Integer}","page":"Home","text":"alloc_period_means(x, sm, np) -> PeriodMeans\n\nNaN32-initialized PeriodMeans for np periods, with the spatial dimensions of x and sm.\n\nExample\n\npm = alloc_period_means(x, sm, 20)\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PlanetPostStats.TimeSeriesMeSd.alloc_period_means"},{"category":"method","location":"#PlanetPostStats.TimeSeriesMeSd.annual_means-Tuple{AbstractArray{<:Real}, PlanetPostStats.TimeSeriesMeSd.SpatialMeans, AbstractVector{PlanetPostStats.TimeSeriesMeSd.YearMonth}, Any}","page":"Home","text":"annual_means(x, sm, months, month_weights; threshold=80.0) -> PeriodMeans\n\nAnnual means of all complete calendar years of the monthly record, for the gridded field x and its zonal and global means sm, computed with PlanetTools.PlanetStatistics.calc_annual_mean_ts!.\n\nDefinitions (PlanetTools): month t gets the weight month_weights[t] times the availability of its input (1 for the gridded field; sm.zm_w, sm.gm_w for the zonal and global means, i.e. months with partly missing spatial coverage get less weight); the mean is NaN if fewer than threshold percent of the 12 months are valid; the availability of the annual mean is the fraction of valid months.\n\nArguments\n\nx::AbstractArray{<:Real}: monthly field (Lon, Lat, [Lev], Time).\nsm::SpatialMeans: its zonal and global means from planet_means.\nmonths::AbstractVector{YearMonth}: labels of the Time dimension (consecutive).\nmonth_weights: weights of the months (length Time), e.g. month_weights(calendar, months), or nothing for equal weights.\n\nKeyword arguments\n\nthreshold::Real = 80.0: minimum percentage of valid months.\n\nReturns\n\nPeriodMeans with one entry per year of annual_periods(months); an empty last dimension if there is no complete year.\n\nExample\n\nw = month_weights(MARS_CALENDAR, months)\nan = annual_means(x, planet_means(x, area), months, w)\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PlanetPostStats.TimeSeriesMeSd.annual_means"},{"category":"method","location":"#PlanetPostStats.TimeSeriesMeSd.annual_periods-Tuple{AbstractVector{PlanetPostStats.TimeSeriesMeSd.YearMonth}}","page":"Home","text":"annual_periods(months::AbstractVector{YearMonth}) -> Vector{Period}\n\nAll complete calendar years (January … December) contained in the monthly record months, which must be consecutive months in chronological order. Partial years at the beginning or end of the record are omitted. Each Period holds the label of the January and the 12 record indices of the year.\n\nExample\n\njulia> months = yearmonth_range(YearMonth(1, 7), YearMonth(3, 12));\n\njulia> [(p.first.year, p.slots) for p in annual_periods(months)]\n2-element Vector{Tuple{Int64, UnitRange{Int64}}}:\n (2, 7:18)\n (3, 19:30)\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PlanetPostStats.TimeSeriesMeSd.annual_periods"},{"category":"method","location":"#PlanetPostStats.TimeSeriesMeSd.annual_summary-Tuple{AbstractVector{PlanetPostStats.TimeSeriesMeSd.RunResult}}","page":"Home","text":"annual_summary(results::AbstractVector{RunResult}) -> DataFrame\n\nConcatenation of the annual tables of all runs (multi-year mean MOA and standard deviation SOA of the annual global means of the 2D variables).\n\nExample\n\nusing DataFrames\ndf = annual_summary(run_timeseries_statistics(cfg))\nfilter(:Varname => ==(\"prsurf\"), df)\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PlanetPostStats.TimeSeriesMeSd.annual_summary"},{"category":"method","location":"#PlanetPostStats.TimeSeriesMeSd.attribute_dict-Tuple{Any}","page":"Home","text":"attribute_dict(attrib) -> OrderedDict{String,Any}\n\nCopies a NetCDF attribute collection into a plain OrderedDict, detached from the (possibly closed) file, so that it stays valid after the file is closed.\n\nExample\n\nNCDataset(\"JAN0001.aijRUN1.nc\") do ds\n    attribute_dict(ds[\"axyp\"].attrib)\nend\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PlanetPostStats.TimeSeriesMeSd.attribute_dict"},{"category":"method","location":"#PlanetPostStats.TimeSeriesMeSd.check_consecutive-Tuple{AbstractVector{PlanetPostStats.TimeSeriesMeSd.YearMonth}}","page":"Home","text":"check_consecutive(months::AbstractVector{YearMonth})\n\nThrows an ArgumentError unless months consists of consecutive months in chronological order (each element one month after its predecessor).\n\nExample\n\njulia> check_consecutive(yearmonth_range(YearMonth(1, 1), YearMonth(1, 6)))  # no error\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PlanetPostStats.TimeSeriesMeSd.check_consecutive"},{"category":"method","location":"#PlanetPostStats.TimeSeriesMeSd.check_pressure_levels-Tuple{AbstractVector{<:Real}}","page":"Home","text":"check_pressure_levels(levels) -> nothing\n\nThrows an ArgumentError unless levels is a non-empty vector of positive, finite, unique pressures.\n\nExample\n\njulia> check_pressure_levels([6.0, 3.0]) === nothing\ntrue\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PlanetPostStats.TimeSeriesMeSd.check_pressure_levels"},{"category":"method","location":"#PlanetPostStats.TimeSeriesMeSd.climatology_slots-Tuple{AbstractVector{PlanetPostStats.TimeSeriesMeSd.YearMonth}, Tuple{PlanetPostStats.TimeSeriesMeSd.YearMonth, PlanetPostStats.TimeSeriesMeSd.YearMonth}}","page":"Home","text":"climatology_slots(months, window) -> Vector{Vector{Int}}\n\nRecord indices of every calendar month (1 … 12) to be used for the multi-year statistics of the annual cycle (mom, som products). Only complete calendar years that lie entirely inside window and inside the record are used, so that each calendar month is sampled the same number of times.\n\nReturns a vector of 12 index vectors; element m contains the indices of month m.\n\nExample\n\njulia> months = yearmonth_range(YearMonth(1, 1), YearMonth(4, 6));\n\njulia> slots = climatology_slots(months, (YearMonth(2, 3), YearMonth(4, 6)));\n\njulia> slots[1]   # only year 3 is a full year inside the window\n1-element Vector{Int64}:\n 25\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PlanetPostStats.TimeSeriesMeSd.climatology_slots"},{"category":"method","location":"#PlanetPostStats.TimeSeriesMeSd.contiguous_range-Tuple{AbstractVector{<:Integer}}","page":"Home","text":"contiguous_range(idx::AbstractVector{<:Integer}) -> UnitRange{Int}\n\nConverts a vector of consecutive indices into a UnitRange (as required by calc_multiyear_stats! with Val(:annual)); throws an ArgumentError if the indices are not consecutive. An empty vector gives an empty range.\n\nExample\n\njulia> contiguous_range([3, 4, 5])\n3:5\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PlanetPostStats.TimeSeriesMeSd.contiguous_range"},{"category":"method","location":"#PlanetPostStats.TimeSeriesMeSd.create_output_file-Tuple{AbstractString, PlanetPostStats.TimeSeriesMeSd.TimeSeriesConfig, PlanetPostStats.TimeSeriesMeSd.RunData, Symbol, Bool}","page":"Home","text":"create_output_file(path, cfg, rd, rep, has_model; has_plev=false, time_cell_method,\n                   time_months=nothing, climatology=false,\n                   extra_attributes=OrderedDict()) -> OutputFile\n\nCreates the NetCDF file path (parent directories are created as needed) with PlanetTools.ReadWritePlanet.writenetcdf and writes dimensions, coordinates, metadata, grid-cell area, and vertical-coordinate scalars. Data variables are added afterwards with write_field!.\n\nContents:\n\ndimensions and coordinates lon, lat, the model-layer dimension (if has_model), the pressure-level dimension plev (if has_plev; hPa, values of output_pressure_levels(cfg)), and, for time series and climatologies, the unlimited dimension time;\nfor time series: time (months from cfg.time_axis.reference to the first month of each period, attributes from time_attributes), the integer variables year(time) and month(time), and the date strings Dates(time) (\"YYYY-MM-01\", as always written by writenetcdf);\nfor climatologies (mom, som): time = 1 … 12 and month(time);\nplm, ple (reference pressures on the vertical dimension) and LS1, Psf, Ptop (if cfg.vertical is set) for files with variables on model levels;\nthe grid-cell area axyp (the name writenetcdf uses): cell areas (ij), the zonal mean of the cell areas (zm), or the total planetary area (gm);\nglobal attributes: Experiment, cfg.global_attributes, Planet, Missing_data_threshold_percent, Seasonal_means_weighted_by_month_length, Standard_deviation, Vertical_interpolation (files with pressure levels), extra_attributes, Software, File_creation_time.\n\nArguments\n\npath::AbstractString: output file path.\ncfg::TimeSeriesConfig: configuration.\nrd::RunData: data of the run (grid, run identifier).\nrep::Symbol: :ij, :zm (lon of length 1, value 0), or :gm (lon and lat of length 1, value 0).\nhas_model::Bool: whether the file will contain variables on model levels.\n\nKeyword arguments\n\nhas_plev::Bool = false: whether the file will contain variables on pressure levels.\ntime_cell_method::AbstractString: temporal part of cell_methods.\ntime_months = nothing: first month of every time step for time-series files.\nclimatology::Bool = false: annual-cycle file with time = 1 … 12.\nextra_attributes: additional global attributes.\n\nExample\n\nof = create_output_file(\"ANN_0003_0020.prsurfRUN1.gm.moa.nc\", cfg, rd, :gm, false;\n                        time_cell_method=\"time: multi-year annual mean\")\nwrite_field!(of, cfg, \"prsurf\", moa, rd.variables[\"prsurf\"].attrib, false)\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PlanetPostStats.TimeSeriesMeSd.create_output_file"},{"category":"method","location":"#PlanetPostStats.TimeSeriesMeSd.cumulative_sums-Tuple{AbstractVector{<:AbstractString}}","page":"Home","text":"cumulative_sums(sources; names, long_names=names, units=\"\") -> Vector{DerivedVariable}\n\nConvenience constructor of a chain of accumulated sums, e.g. over size bins: for sources = [s₁, s₂, …, sₙ] it returns n - 1 derived variables\n\nnames[1] = s₁ + s₂,  names[2] = s₁ + s₂ + s₃,  …,  names[n-1] = s₁ + … + sₙ.\n\nEach derived variable is defined as the previous one plus the next bin, so that the total work is linear in n.\n\nArguments\n\nsources::AbstractVector{<:AbstractString}: names of the size-bin variables, ordered from the smallest to the largest bin (length(sources) ≥ 2).\n\nKeyword arguments\n\nnames: n - 1 names of the accumulated variables.\nlong_names = names: n - 1 descriptive names.\nunits = \"\": units (empty → units of sources[1]).\n\nExample\n\njulia> ds = cumulative_sums([\"Clay\", \"Silt1\", \"Silt2\"];\n                            names=[\"Clay_Silt1\", \"Clay_Silt2\"], units=\"kg kg-1\");\n\njulia> [(d.name, d.sources) for d in ds]\n2-element Vector{Tuple{String, Vector{String}}}:\n (\"Clay_Silt1\", [\"Clay\", \"Silt1\"])\n (\"Clay_Silt2\", [\"Clay_Silt1\", \"Silt2\"])\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PlanetPostStats.TimeSeriesMeSd.cumulative_sums"},{"category":"method","location":"#PlanetPostStats.TimeSeriesMeSd.days_in_year-Tuple{PlanetPostStats.TimeSeriesMeSd.PlanetCalendar}","page":"Home","text":"days_in_year(cal::PlanetCalendar) -> Float64\n\nSum of the 12 month lengths of the calendar.\n\nExample\n\njulia> days_in_year(MARS_CALENDAR)\n669.0\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PlanetPostStats.TimeSeriesMeSd.days_in_year"},{"category":"method","location":"#PlanetPostStats.TimeSeriesMeSd.default_pressure_levels-Tuple{AbstractString}","page":"Home","text":"default_pressure_levels(planet::AbstractString) -> Vector{Float64}\n\nDefault output pressure levels (hPa) of planet (case-insensitive) from DEFAULT_PRESSURE_LEVELS; throws an ArgumentError if no default is defined for the planet.\n\nExample\n\njulia> default_pressure_levels(\"Mars\")[1:3]\n3-element Vector{Float64}:\n 18.789\n 16.582\n 14.633\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PlanetPostStats.TimeSeriesMeSd.default_pressure_levels"},{"category":"method","location":"#PlanetPostStats.TimeSeriesMeSd.dust_mass_classes-Tuple{Any}","page":"Home","text":"dust_mass_classes(available; physvar=\"\", addlongname=\"\", units=\"\") -> Vector{DerivedVariable}\n\nCumulative dust mass size classes of ModelE/ROCKE-3D, with the bin and class names of PlanetTools.DerivePhysicsVariablesModelE.accumulate_dust_masses_modele:\n\nclass sum of the bins\nPM2Dust Clay\nPM4Dust Clay + Silt1\nPM8Dust Clay + Silt1 + Silt2\nPM16Dust … + Silt3\nPM32Dust … + Silt4\nPM64Dust … + Silt5\n\nThe bin variables are named <bin><physvar> and the classes <class><physvar>. As in PlanetTools, the accumulation stops at the first bin not contained in available, so only complete classes are created. The long name of a class is \"<class> <addlongname>\" (or \"<class>\"), the units are those of Clay<physvar> unless units is given.\n\nThe bins and classes are taken from PlanetTools, so both packages stay consistent.\n\nArguments\n\navailable: names of the variables that will be loaded, typically [v.name for g in groups for v in g.variables].\n\nKeyword arguments\n\nphysvar::AbstractString = \"\": suffix of the bin names (e.g. \"_emission\").\naddlongname::AbstractString = \"\": text appended to the class name in long_name.\nunits::AbstractString = \"\": units of the classes (empty → units of the clay bin).\n\nExample\n\njulia> ds = dust_mass_classes([\"Clay\", \"Silt1\", \"Silt2\", \"Silt3\", \"Silt4\"]);\n\njulia> [(d.name, d.sources) for d in ds][1:3]\n3-element Vector{Tuple{String, Vector{String}}}:\n (\"PM2Dust\", [\"Clay\"])\n (\"PM4Dust\", [\"PM2Dust\", \"Silt1\"])\n (\"PM8Dust\", [\"PM4Dust\", \"Silt2\"])\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PlanetPostStats.TimeSeriesMeSd.dust_mass_classes"},{"category":"method","location":"#PlanetPostStats.TimeSeriesMeSd.fromabsmonth-Tuple{Integer}","page":"Home","text":"fromabsmonth(n::Integer) -> YearMonth\n\nInverse of absmonth: converts an absolute month counter back into a YearMonth. Works for negative counters (years before year 0) as well.\n\nExample\n\njulia> fromabsmonth(35)\nYearMonth(2, 12)\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PlanetPostStats.TimeSeriesMeSd.fromabsmonth"},{"category":"method","location":"#PlanetPostStats.TimeSeriesMeSd.input_filename-Tuple{PlanetPostStats.TimeSeriesMeSd.TimeSeriesConfig, PlanetPostStats.TimeSeriesMeSd.YearMonth, Any, Any}","page":"Home","text":"input_filename(cfg::TimeSeriesConfig, ym, product, run) -> String\n\nFile name of the scaleacc file of product for month ym and run run, using cfg.filename or, if that is nothing, scaleacc_filename.\n\nExample\n\njulia> input_filename(cfg, YearMonth(1, 1), \"aij\", \"RUN1\")\n\"JAN0001.aijRUN1.nc\"\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PlanetPostStats.TimeSeriesMeSd.input_filename"},{"category":"method","location":"#PlanetPostStats.TimeSeriesMeSd.interpolate_to_pressure-Tuple{AbstractArray{<:Real, 4}, AbstractArray{<:Real, 3}, AbstractVector{<:Real}, PlanetPostStats.TimeSeriesMeSd.VerticalCoordinate, AbstractVector{<:Real}}","page":"Home","text":"interpolate_to_pressure(x, ps, plm, vc, plev) -> Array{Float32,4}\n\nInterpolates the monthly 3D field x from the model layers to the pressure levels plev.\n\nFor every column and month, the mid-layer pressures p₁ > p₂ > … > p_L of the model layers are computed from the surface pressure ps of that column and month with layer_pressure. For a pressure level P:\n\nP > ps (below the local surface): missing (NaN32);\nps ≥ P ≥ p₁ (between the surface and the mid-point of the lowest layer): value of the lowest layer;\np_l ≥ P ≥ p_{l+1}: linear interpolation in ln p between layers l and l + 1, x = x_l + (ln P − ln p_l) / (ln p_{l+1} − ln p_l) · (x_{l+1} − x_l);\nP < p_L (above the mid-point of the uppermost layer): missing.\n\nThe result is missing where a value of the two bracketing layers or the surface pressure is missing. The loop over the columns is multi-threaded.\n\nArguments\n\nx::AbstractArray{<:Real,4}: field (lon, lat, layer, time), layer 1 at the bottom; missing values NaN.\nps::AbstractArray{<:Real,3}: surface pressure (lon, lat, time), same unit as plm and plev (hPa).\nplm::AbstractVector{<:Real}: reference mid-layer pressures of the layers.\nvc::VerticalCoordinate: parameters of the vertical coordinate.\nplev::AbstractVector{<:Real}: target pressure levels.\n\nReturns\n\nArray{Float32,4} of size (lon, lat, length(plev), time).\n\nExample\n\njulia> vc = VerticalCoordinate(3, 10.0, 1.0);   # layers 1, 2 σ; layer 3 pressure\n\njulia> plm = [9.0, 5.0, 0.5];\n\njulia> x = reshape(Float32[log(9.0), log(5.0), log(0.5)], 1, 1, 3, 1);  # x = ln p\n\njulia> ps = fill(10.0f0, 1, 1, 1);\n\njulia> y = interpolate_to_pressure(x, ps, plm, vc, [12.0, 9.5, 7.0, 2.0, 0.1]);\n\njulia> isnan(y[1]), y[2] ≈ log(9.0), y[3] ≈ log(7.0), y[4] ≈ log(2.0), isnan(y[5])\n(true, true, true, true, true)\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PlanetPostStats.TimeSeriesMeSd.interpolate_to_pressure"},{"category":"method","location":"#PlanetPostStats.TimeSeriesMeSd.layer_pressure-Tuple{Real, Real, Integer, PlanetPostStats.TimeSeriesMeSd.VerticalCoordinate}","page":"Home","text":"layer_pressure(ps, plm_l, l, vc::VerticalCoordinate) -> Float64\n\nMid-layer pressure of model layer l in a column with surface pressure ps.\n\nFor the σ layers (l < vc.ls1) the pressure follows the surface pressure, p = p_top + σ (ps − p_top) with σ = (plm_l − p_top) / (p_sf − p_top), where plm_l is the reference mid-layer pressure of the layer (plm in the input files) and p_sf, p_top are vc.psf and vc.ptop. For the pure pressure layers (l ≥ vc.ls1) the pressure is plm_l. All pressures are in the same unit (hPa).\n\nArguments\n\nps::Real: surface pressure of the column.\nplm_l::Real: reference mid-layer pressure of layer l.\nl::Integer: layer index (1 = lowest layer).\nvc::VerticalCoordinate: parameters of the vertical coordinate.\n\nExample\n\njulia> vc = VerticalCoordinate(31, 6.86, 0.2);\n\njulia> layer_pressure(6.86, 5.0, 1, vc)      # reference column: plm itself\n5.0\n\njulia> layer_pressure(8.0, 5.0, 1, vc) ≈ 0.2 + 4.8 * 7.8 / 6.66\ntrue\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PlanetPostStats.TimeSeriesMeSd.layer_pressure"},{"category":"method","location":"#PlanetPostStats.TimeSeriesMeSd.lift-Tuple{AbstractArray}","page":"Home","text":"lift(a) -> AbstractArray\nlift(nothing) -> nothing\n\nAdds two leading singleton dimensions (Sim = 1, Var = 1) to a without copying, for calls of PlanetTools functions. nothing is passed through.\n\nExample\n\njulia> size(lift(zeros(4, 3, 10)))\n(1, 1, 4, 3, 10)\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PlanetPostStats.TimeSeriesMeSd.lift"},{"category":"method","location":"#PlanetPostStats.TimeSeriesMeSd.load_run-Tuple{PlanetPostStats.TimeSeriesMeSd.TimeSeriesConfig, AbstractString}","page":"Home","text":"load_run(cfg::TimeSeriesConfig, run::AbstractString) -> RunData\n\nReads all variables of all input groups of run for every month of cfg.sim_period into memory, applies the variable scale factors, and evaluates the derived variables.\n\nProcedure\n\nConstructs the expected input path of every (group, month) and checks which files exist. The monthly record ends with the last month for which any file exists; months with missing files inside the record are kept as NaN32 (gaps).\nProbes the first available file of each group for the variables, their dimensionality and attributes, and the grid (coordinates, cell area axyp).\nReads every file once (one open per file, all variables of the group) and stores each variable at a fixed position, independent of which files exist.\nEvaluates cfg.derived in order.\n\nMemory: 4 × nlon × nlat × (n2d + nlev × n3d) × nmonths bytes for one run (e.g. ≈ 0.9 GB for 72 × 46 × 40, seven 3D variables, 240 months). Only one run is held in memory at a time by run_timeseries_statistics.\n\nArguments\n\ncfg::TimeSeriesConfig: the configuration.\nrun::AbstractString: run identifier (one of cfg.runs).\n\nReturns\n\nA RunData.\n\nExample\n\nrd = load_run(cfg, \"MarsDustRun1\")\nrd.months[end]                          # last month with data\nsize(rd.variables[\"Clay\"].data)         # (72, 46, 40, 240)\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PlanetPostStats.TimeSeriesMeSd.load_run"},{"category":"method","location":"#PlanetPostStats.TimeSeriesMeSd.month_weights-Tuple{PlanetPostStats.TimeSeriesMeSd.PlanetCalendar, AbstractVector{PlanetPostStats.TimeSeriesMeSd.YearMonth}}","page":"Home","text":"month_weights(cal::PlanetCalendar, months::AbstractVector{YearMonth}) -> Vector{Float64}\n\nWeight of every month in months for temporal averaging: the month length divided by the length of the year. For a complete year the weights add up to one.\n\nExample\n\njulia> w = month_weights(MARS_CALENDAR, yearmonth_range(YearMonth(1, 1), YearMonth(1, 12)));\n\njulia> sum(w) ≈ 1\ntrue\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PlanetPostStats.TimeSeriesMeSd.month_weights"},{"category":"method","location":"#PlanetPostStats.TimeSeriesMeSd.monthly_stats-Tuple{AbstractArray{<:Real}, Any, AbstractVector{<:AbstractVector{<:Integer}}}","page":"Home","text":"monthly_stats(x, x_w, slots12; threshold=80.0, corrected=true) -> (mean, sd, avail)\n\nMulti-year mean and standard deviation of each calendar month of the annual cycle, computed with PlanetTools.PlanetStatistics.calc_multiyear_stats! (Val(:monthly)), with the same definitions as multiyear_stats applied month by month.\n\nArguments\n\nx::AbstractArray{<:Real}: monthly field, time as last dimension.\nx_w: availability weights of x (e.g. sm.zm_w for zonal means), or nothing.\nslots12::AbstractVector{<:AbstractVector{<:Integer}}: 12 index vectors, see climatology_slots.\n\nKeyword arguments\n\nthreshold::Real = 80.0: minimum percentage of valid samples per month.\ncorrected::Bool = true: sample (true) or population (false) standard deviation.\n\nReturns\n\nArrays with the leading dimensions of x and 12 as last dimension.\n\nExample\n\nme, sd, av = monthly_stats(sm.gm, sm.gm_w, climatology_slots(months, window))\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PlanetPostStats.TimeSeriesMeSd.monthly_stats"},{"category":"method","location":"#PlanetPostStats.TimeSeriesMeSd.monthname-Tuple{PlanetPostStats.TimeSeriesMeSd.PlanetCalendar, PlanetPostStats.TimeSeriesMeSd.YearMonth}","page":"Home","text":"monthname(cal::PlanetCalendar, ym::YearMonth) -> String\n\nThree-letter label of the month of ym in calendar cal (e.g. \"JAN\").\n\nExample\n\njulia> monthname(MARS_CALENDAR, YearMonth(4, 12))\n\"DEC\"\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PlanetPostStats.TimeSeriesMeSd.monthname"},{"category":"method","location":"#PlanetPostStats.TimeSeriesMeSd.months_between-Tuple{PlanetPostStats.TimeSeriesMeSd.YearMonth, PlanetPostStats.TimeSeriesMeSd.YearMonth}","page":"Home","text":"months_between(a::YearMonth, b::YearMonth) -> Int\n\nNumber of months from a to b (b - a); negative if b precedes a.\n\nExample\n\njulia> months_between(YearMonth(1, 1), YearMonth(20, 12))\n239\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PlanetPostStats.TimeSeriesMeSd.months_between"},{"category":"method","location":"#PlanetPostStats.TimeSeriesMeSd.multiyear_stats-Tuple{AbstractArray{<:Real}, Any, AbstractUnitRange{<:Integer}}","page":"Home","text":"multiyear_stats(x, x_w, slots; threshold=80.0, corrected=true) -> (mean, sd, avail)\n\nMulti-year mean and standard deviation over the contiguous samples slots (last dimension of x, e.g. the annual or seasonal means of the years in the statistics window), computed with PlanetTools.PlanetStatistics.calc_multiyear_stats! (Val(:annual)).\n\nDefinitions (PlanetTools): with the availabilities x_w as weights w of the valid samples, V₁ = Σw, V₂ = Σw², the mean is μ = Σwx / V₁ and the standard deviation\n\ncorrected=true (default): σ = √(Σw(x − μ)² / (V₁ − V₂/V₁)), the sample standard deviation for reliability weights, √(Σ(x − μ)² / (n − 1)) for equal weights; NaN with fewer than two valid samples;\ncorrected=false: the population standard deviation √(Σw(x − μ)² / V₁).\n\nResults are NaN if fewer than threshold percent of the samples are valid; avail is the fraction of valid samples.\n\nArguments\n\nx::AbstractArray{<:Real}: samples along the last dimension.\nx_w: availability weights of x (same size) or nothing (equal weights).\nslots::AbstractUnitRange{<:Integer}: indices of the samples to use.\n\nKeyword arguments\n\nthreshold::Real = 80.0: minimum percentage of valid samples.\ncorrected::Bool = true: sample (true) or population (false) standard deviation.\n\nExample\n\njulia> me, sd, av = multiyear_stats(reshape(Float32[1, 2, 3, NaN], 1, 4), nothing, 1:4;\n                                    threshold=50);\n\njulia> me[1], sd[1], av[1]\n(2.0f0, 1.0f0, 0.75f0)\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PlanetPostStats.TimeSeriesMeSd.multiyear_stats"},{"category":"method","location":"#PlanetPostStats.TimeSeriesMeSd.nanarray-Tuple","page":"Home","text":"nanarray(dims...) -> Array{Float32}\n\nFloat32 array of size dims filled with NaN32. PlanetTools leaves output entries not covered by a calculation unchanged, so outputs are initialized with NaN.\n\nExample\n\njulia> all(isnan, nanarray(2, 3))\ntrue\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PlanetPostStats.TimeSeriesMeSd.nanarray"},{"category":"method","location":"#PlanetPostStats.TimeSeriesMeSd.output_directory-Tuple{PlanetPostStats.TimeSeriesMeSd.TimeSeriesConfig, AbstractString}","page":"Home","text":"output_directory(cfg::TimeSeriesConfig, run::AbstractString) -> String\n\nDirectory into which the output of run is written: joinpath(cfg.simpath, run, cfg.output_dir), or joinpath(cfg.output_root, run, cfg.output_dir) if cfg.output_root is set.\n\nExample\n\njulia> output_directory(cfg, \"RUN1\")\n\"/data/sims/RUN1/Tracermass3d\"\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PlanetPostStats.TimeSeriesMeSd.output_directory"},{"category":"method","location":"#PlanetPostStats.TimeSeriesMeSd.output_entries-Tuple{PlanetPostStats.TimeSeriesMeSd.TimeSeriesConfig, PlanetPostStats.TimeSeriesMeSd.RunData}","page":"Home","text":"output_entries(cfg::TimeSeriesConfig, rd::RunData) -> Vector{OutputEntry}\n\nAssigns the variables of a run to the output file sets and vertical coordinates:\n\nwithout cfg.pressure_levels: all variables in :main, 3D variables on model levels;\nmode = :add: all variables in :main as above, plus every 3D variable with to_pressure = true on pressure levels in :pressure;\nmode = :replace: all variables in :main, 3D variables with to_pressure = true on pressure levels, the other 3D variables on model levels.\n\nThe pressure-level fields are computed with interpolate_to_pressure from the monthly surface pressure cfg.pressure_levels.surface_pressure of the run.\n\nExample\n\nentries = output_entries(cfg, rd)\ncount(e -> e.vertical == :pressure, entries)\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PlanetPostStats.TimeSeriesMeSd.output_entries"},{"category":"method","location":"#PlanetPostStats.TimeSeriesMeSd.output_filename-Tuple{AbstractString, PlanetPostStats.TimeSeriesMeSd.TimeSeriesConfig, PlanetPostStats.TimeSeriesMeSd.RunData, Symbol, AbstractString}","page":"Home","text":"output_filename(kind, cfg, rd, rep, vtag; prefix) -> String\n\nOutput file name <prefix>.<output_name><run>.<tag>.<kind>.nc, with tag = rep_tag(rep, vtag) and kind one of mts, ats, sts, moa, soa, mos, sos, mom, som.\n\nExample\n\njulia> output_filename(\"moa\", cfg, rd, :gm, \"\"; prefix=\"ANN_0003_0020\")\n\"ANN_0003_0020.prsurfRUN1.gm.moa.nc\"\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PlanetPostStats.TimeSeriesMeSd.output_filename"},{"category":"method","location":"#PlanetPostStats.TimeSeriesMeSd.output_pressure_levels-Tuple{PlanetPostStats.TimeSeriesMeSd.TimeSeriesConfig}","page":"Home","text":"output_pressure_levels(cfg::TimeSeriesConfig) -> Vector{Float64}\n\nPressure levels (hPa) of the output: the explicit levels of cfg.pressure_levels, or, if those are nothing, the default levels of the planet cfg.calendar.name (default_pressure_levels). Throws an ArgumentError if cfg.pressure_levels is not set or no default exists for the planet.\n\nExample\n\njulia> cfg = TimeSeriesConfig(; cfg_kwargs..., calendar=MARS_CALENDAR,\n                              pressure_levels=PressureLevels());\n\njulia> length(output_pressure_levels(cfg))\n43\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PlanetPostStats.TimeSeriesMeSd.output_pressure_levels"},{"category":"method","location":"#PlanetPostStats.TimeSeriesMeSd.period_in_window-Tuple{PlanetPostStats.TimeSeriesMeSd.Period, AbstractVector{PlanetPostStats.TimeSeriesMeSd.YearMonth}, Tuple{PlanetPostStats.TimeSeriesMeSd.YearMonth, PlanetPostStats.TimeSeriesMeSd.YearMonth}}","page":"Home","text":"period_in_window(p::Period, months, window::Tuple{YearMonth,YearMonth}) -> Bool\n\ntrue if all months of period p (indices into the monthly record months) lie inside the closed interval window = (first, last).\n\nExample\n\njulia> months = yearmonth_range(YearMonth(1, 1), YearMonth(3, 12));\n\njulia> ps = annual_periods(months);\n\njulia> [period_in_window(p, months, (YearMonth(2, 1), YearMonth(3, 12))) for p in ps]\n3-element Vector{Bool}:\n 0\n 1\n 1\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PlanetPostStats.TimeSeriesMeSd.period_in_window"},{"category":"function","location":"#PlanetPostStats.TimeSeriesMeSd.period_label","page":"Home","text":"period_label(months, periods) -> String\n\n\"YYYY-YYYY\" label with the years of the first months of the first and last period.\n\nExample\n\njulia> months = yearmonth_range(YearMonth(1, 1), YearMonth(3, 12));\n\njulia> period_label(months, annual_periods(months))\n\"0001-0003\"\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PlanetPostStats.TimeSeriesMeSd.period_label"},{"category":"method","location":"#PlanetPostStats.TimeSeriesMeSd.planet_means-Tuple{AbstractArray{<:Real}, AbstractMatrix{<:Real}}","page":"Home","text":"planet_means(x, area; threshold=80.0) -> SpatialMeans\n\nZonal means and area-weighted global means of the monthly field x, computed with PlanetTools.PlanetStatistics.calc_planet_means!.\n\nDefinitions (PlanetTools): the zonal mean averages the valid longitudes with equal weights, its availability is the fraction of valid longitudes; the global mean is weighted by the cell areas area, its availability is the valid area fraction. A mean is NaN (availability 0) if the availability is below threshold percent.\n\nThe PlanetTools kernel loops over the data without temporary arrays and is multi-threaded over levels and time steps.\n\nArguments\n\nx::AbstractArray{<:Real}: (Lon, Lat, Time) or (Lon, Lat, Lev, Time), missing values NaN.\narea::AbstractMatrix{<:Real}: cell areas (Lon, Lat) (axyp).\n\nKeyword arguments\n\nthreshold::Real = 80.0: minimum valid percentage (longitudes or area).\n\nExample\n\njulia> x = reshape(Float32[1, 3, 2, NaN], 2, 2, 1);\n\njulia> sm = planet_means(x, [1.0 3.0; 1.0 3.0]; threshold=0);\n\njulia> vec(sm.zm), sm.gm[1], sm.gm_w[1]\n(Float32[2.0, 2.0], 2.0f0, 0.625f0)\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PlanetPostStats.TimeSeriesMeSd.planet_means"},{"category":"method","location":"#PlanetPostStats.TimeSeriesMeSd.pressure_flags-Tuple{PlanetPostStats.TimeSeriesMeSd.TimeSeriesConfig}","page":"Home","text":"pressure_flags(cfg::TimeSeriesConfig) -> Dict{String,Bool}\n\nto_pressure flag of every configured variable (input and derived), by name.\n\nExample\n\njulia> pressure_flags(cfg)[\"airmass\"]\nfalse\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PlanetPostStats.TimeSeriesMeSd.pressure_flags"},{"category":"method","location":"#PlanetPostStats.TimeSeriesMeSd.process_run-Tuple{PlanetPostStats.TimeSeriesMeSd.TimeSeriesConfig, String}","page":"Home","text":"process_run(cfg::TimeSeriesConfig, run::String) -> RunResult\n\nProcesses a single run (see run_timeseries_statistics for the steps).\n\nExample\n\nres = process_run(cfg, \"MarsDustRun1\")\nres.files\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PlanetPostStats.TimeSeriesMeSd.process_run"},{"category":"method","location":"#PlanetPostStats.TimeSeriesMeSd.read_coordinate-Tuple{Any, AbstractString}","page":"Home","text":"read_coordinate(ds, name) -> Union{Nothing,Vector{Float32}}\n\nReads the one-dimensional variable name from the open dataset ds as Float32 (missing values become NaN32); returns nothing if it does not exist.\n\nExample\n\nNCDataset(\"JAN0001.aijlRUN1.nc\") do ds\n    read_coordinate(ds, \"plm\")\nend\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PlanetPostStats.TimeSeriesMeSd.read_coordinate"},{"category":"method","location":"#PlanetPostStats.TimeSeriesMeSd.rep_tag-Tuple{Symbol, AbstractString}","page":"Home","text":"rep_tag(rep::Symbol, vtag::AbstractString) -> String\n\nFile-name tag of the spatial representation rep (:ij, :zm, :gm) followed by the vertical tag vtag: \"\" for files with only 2D variables, \"l\" for files with variables on model levels, \"p\" for files with variables on pressure levels only.\n\nExample\n\njulia> rep_tag(:zm, \"l\"), rep_tag(:gm, \"p\"), rep_tag(:ij, \"\")\n(\"zml\", \"gmp\", \"ij\")\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PlanetPostStats.TimeSeriesMeSd.rep_tag"},{"category":"method","location":"#PlanetPostStats.TimeSeriesMeSd.run_timeseries_statistics-Tuple{PlanetPostStats.TimeSeriesMeSd.TimeSeriesConfig}","page":"Home","text":"run_timeseries_statistics(cfg::TimeSeriesConfig; runs=cfg.runs) -> Vector{RunResult}\n\nMain entry point. Validates cfg and processes every run in runs (default: all runs of the configuration) sequentially:\n\nload_run reads the monthly scaleacc files and evaluates derived variables.\nWith cfg.pressure_levels, the 3D variables with to_pressure = true are interpolated to pressure levels (interpolate_to_pressure), one variable at a time, and assigned to the output files (output_entries).\nFor every variable, the monthly gridded field (ij), its zonal mean (zm), and its global mean (gm) are formed (planet_means); for each of the three, the requested products of ALL_PRODUCTS are computed (annual_means, seasonal_means, multiyear_stats, monthly_stats, all built on PlanetTools.PlanetStatistics) and written immediately, so that only one variable's results are held in memory.\nThe run's data are released before the next run is loaded.\n\nOutput directory of run r: output_directory(cfg, r), with subdirectories MonthlyTs, AnnualTs, SeasonalTs, AnnualMeSd, SeasonalMeSd, MonthlyMeSd.\n\nStatistics are computed only from periods lying entirely in cfg.stat_period; products for which no such period exists in a run (e.g. a run shorter than the window) are skipped with a warning.\n\nArguments\n\ncfg::TimeSeriesConfig: configuration.\n\nKeyword arguments\n\nruns = cfg.runs: subset of runs to process.\n\nReturns\n\nVector{RunResult}, one per run, with written file paths and summary tables (see annual_summary, seasonal_summary).\n\nExample\n\nusing PlanetPostStats.TimeSeriesMeSd\nresults = run_timeseries_statistics(cfg)\nannual_summary(results)\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PlanetPostStats.TimeSeriesMeSd.run_timeseries_statistics"},{"category":"method","location":"#PlanetPostStats.TimeSeriesMeSd.scaleacc_filename-Tuple{PlanetPostStats.TimeSeriesMeSd.YearMonth, AbstractString, AbstractString}","page":"Home","text":"scaleacc_filename(ym::YearMonth, product, run; ext=\".nc\") -> String\n\nDefault name of a monthly scaleacc output file, <MON><YYYY>.<product><run><ext> (e.g. JAN0001.aijMarsDustRun1.nc), built with PlanetTools.Constructors.fnames_modele (upper-case English month abbreviation, year zero-padded to four digits, year ≥ 0).\n\nIf your files follow a different convention, pass any function with the call signature (ym::YearMonth, product::String, run::String) -> String as TimeSeriesConfig.filename.\n\nExample\n\njulia> scaleacc_filename(YearMonth(1, 2), \"taijl\", \"RUN1\")\n\"FEB0001.taijlRUN1.nc\"\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PlanetPostStats.TimeSeriesMeSd.scaleacc_filename"},{"category":"method","location":"#PlanetPostStats.TimeSeriesMeSd.season_months-Tuple{PlanetPostStats.TimeSeriesMeSd.SeasonSpec}","page":"Home","text":"season_months(s::SeasonSpec) -> Vector{Int}\n\nCalendar months (1 … 12) belonging to season s, in chronological order.\n\nExample\n\njulia> season_months(SeasonSpec(\"DJF\", 12, 3))\n3-element Vector{Int64}:\n 12\n  1\n  2\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PlanetPostStats.TimeSeriesMeSd.season_months"},{"category":"method","location":"#PlanetPostStats.TimeSeriesMeSd.seasonal_means-Tuple{AbstractArray{<:Real}, PlanetPostStats.TimeSeriesMeSd.SpatialMeans, AbstractVector{PlanetPostStats.TimeSeriesMeSd.YearMonth}, PlanetPostStats.TimeSeriesMeSd.SeasonSpec, Any}","page":"Home","text":"seasonal_means(x, sm, months, season, month_weights; threshold=80.0) -> PeriodMeans\n\nMeans over all complete occurrences of season in the monthly record, for the gridded field x and its zonal and global means sm, computed with PlanetTools.PlanetStatistics.calc_seasonal_mean_ts!. Weighting, availability, and threshold are defined as for annual_means, with the months of the season in place of the 12 months of a year.\n\nArguments\n\nx, sm, months: as for annual_means.\nseason::SeasonSpec: the season.\nmonth_weights: weights of the months, or nothing for equal weights.\n\nKeyword arguments\n\nthreshold::Real = 80.0: minimum percentage of valid months of a season.\n\nReturns\n\nPeriodMeans with one entry per element of seasonal_periods(months, season).\n\nExample\n\nse = seasonal_means(x, sm, months, SeasonSpec(\"FMA\", 2, 3), w)\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PlanetPostStats.TimeSeriesMeSd.seasonal_means"},{"category":"method","location":"#PlanetPostStats.TimeSeriesMeSd.seasonal_periods-Tuple{AbstractVector{PlanetPostStats.TimeSeriesMeSd.YearMonth}, PlanetPostStats.TimeSeriesMeSd.SeasonSpec}","page":"Home","text":"seasonal_periods(months::AbstractVector{YearMonth}, season::SeasonSpec) -> Vector{Period}\n\nAll complete occurrences of season in the monthly record months (consecutive months in chronological order). An occurrence is complete if all season.length months are inside the record; seasons wrapping into the next year (e.g. NDJ) are therefore only included if the January of the following year is part of the record.\n\nExample\n\njulia> months = yearmonth_range(YearMonth(1, 1), YearMonth(2, 12));\n\njulia> [(p.first, p.slots) for p in seasonal_periods(months, SeasonSpec(\"NDJ\", 11, 3))]\n1-element Vector{Tuple{YearMonth, UnitRange{Int64}}}:\n (YearMonth(1, 11), 11:13)\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PlanetPostStats.TimeSeriesMeSd.seasonal_periods"},{"category":"method","location":"#PlanetPostStats.TimeSeriesMeSd.seasonal_summary-Tuple{AbstractVector{PlanetPostStats.TimeSeriesMeSd.RunResult}}","page":"Home","text":"seasonal_summary(results::AbstractVector{RunResult}) -> DataFrame\n\nConcatenation of the seasonal tables of all runs (multi-year mean MOS and standard deviation SOS of the seasonal global means of the 2D variables).\n\nExample\n\nusing DataFrames\ndf = seasonal_summary(run_timeseries_statistics(cfg))\nfilter([:Varname, :Season] => (v, s) -> v == \"prsurf\" && s == \"FMA\", df)\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PlanetPostStats.TimeSeriesMeSd.seasonal_summary"},{"category":"method","location":"#PlanetPostStats.TimeSeriesMeSd.software_version-Tuple{}","page":"Home","text":"software_version() -> String\n\nName and version of this package, written as global attribute Software.\n\nExample\n\njulia> startswith(software_version(), \"PlanetPostStats.TimeSeriesMeSd\")\ntrue\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PlanetPostStats.TimeSeriesMeSd.software_version"},{"category":"method","location":"#PlanetPostStats.TimeSeriesMeSd.spatial_shape-Tuple{Any, AbstractString}","page":"Home","text":"spatial_shape(ds, name) -> (dims::Vector{String}, shape::Vector{Int})\n\nNames and sizes of the spatial dimensions of variable name in the open dataset ds, excluding singleton time-like dimensions (see TIME_LIKE_DIMS). Throws an ArgumentError if the variable has fewer than 2 or more than 3 spatial dimensions.\n\nExample\n\nNCDataset(\"JAN0001.aijlRUN1.nc\") do ds\n    spatial_shape(ds, \"z\")     # ([\"lon\", \"lat\", \"level\"], [72, 46, 40])\nend\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PlanetPostStats.TimeSeriesMeSd.spatial_shape"},{"category":"method","location":"#PlanetPostStats.TimeSeriesMeSd.sum_of-Tuple{}","page":"Home","text":"sum_of() -> Function\n\nReturns a function that adds an arbitrary number of equally sized arrays element-wise ((a, b, …) -> a .+ b .+ …). A NaN in any summand makes the sum NaN (missing), i.e. a sum over size bins is only valid where all bins are valid.\n\nExample\n\njulia> f = sum_of();\n\njulia> f([1f0, 2f0], [10f0, NaN32])\n2-element Vector{Float32}:\n  11.0\n NaN\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PlanetPostStats.TimeSeriesMeSd.sum_of"},{"category":"method","location":"#PlanetPostStats.TimeSeriesMeSd.time_attributes-Tuple{PlanetPostStats.TimeSeriesMeSd.TimeSeriesConfig}","page":"Home","text":"time_attributes(cfg::TimeSeriesConfig) -> OrderedDict{String,Any}\n\nAttributes of the time coordinate of the time-series files: units from cfg.time_axis, and the CF attributes of the model calendar, calendar (cfg.calendar.cf_calendar) and month_lengths (CF user-defined calendar), plus day_length if set. With a non-standard calendar (e.g. \"mars\"), CF-aware readers, including PlanetTools.ReadWritePlanet.readnetcdf, return the numerical time values instead of misinterpreting them as Earth dates.\n\nExample\n\njulia> time_attributes(TimeSeriesConfig(; cfg_kwargs..., calendar=MARS_CALENDAR))[\"calendar\"]\n\"mars\"\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PlanetPostStats.TimeSeriesMeSd.time_attributes"},{"category":"method","location":"#PlanetPostStats.TimeSeriesMeSd.time_value-Tuple{PlanetPostStats.TimeSeriesMeSd.TimeAxis, PlanetPostStats.TimeSeriesMeSd.YearMonth}","page":"Home","text":"time_value(ax::TimeAxis, first_month::YearMonth) -> Int\n\nNumerical time coordinate of a period starting in first_month, see TimeAxis.\n\nExample\n\njulia> time_value(TimeAxis(), YearMonth(1, 1))\n1\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PlanetPostStats.TimeSeriesMeSd.time_value"},{"category":"function","location":"#PlanetPostStats.TimeSeriesMeSd.unlift","page":"Home","text":"unlift(a, n=2) -> AbstractArray\n\nRemoves the n leading singleton dimensions of a (inverse of lift; n = 3 also removes the Season dimension of seasonal arrays), without copying.\n\nExample\n\njulia> size(unlift(zeros(1, 1, 4, 3)))\n(4, 3)\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PlanetPostStats.TimeSeriesMeSd.unlift"},{"category":"method","location":"#PlanetPostStats.TimeSeriesMeSd.validate_config-Tuple{PlanetPostStats.TimeSeriesMeSd.TimeSeriesConfig}","page":"Home","text":"validate_config(cfg::TimeSeriesConfig) -> TimeSeriesConfig\n\nChecks a configuration for consistency and throws an ArgumentError describing the first problem found. Checks: non-empty runs and groups; unique variable names; sources of derived variables defined before use; valid simulation and statistics periods, with the statistics window overlapping the simulation period; threshold in (0, 100]; known products; deflatelevel in 0:9; for pressure_levels, a vertical coordinate, default levels for the planet if no levels are given, and a configured surface-pressure variable; no reserved names (lon, lat, level, plev, time, year, month, plm, ple, area variable, axyp, Dates, LS1, Psf, Ptop) used as variable names. Returns cfg so that it can be chained.\n\nExample\n\njulia> validate_config(cfg);  # throws if cfg is inconsistent\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PlanetPostStats.TimeSeriesMeSd.validate_config"},{"category":"method","location":"#PlanetPostStats.TimeSeriesMeSd.variable_names-Tuple{PlanetPostStats.TimeSeriesMeSd.TimeSeriesConfig}","page":"Home","text":"variable_names(cfg::TimeSeriesConfig) -> Vector{String}\n\nNames of all variables of the configuration, input variables first (in group order), followed by derived variables, i.e. the order of the variables in the output files.\n\nExample\n\njulia> variable_names(cfg)\n3-element Vector{String}:\n \"prsurf\"\n \"z\"\n \"airmass\"\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PlanetPostStats.TimeSeriesMeSd.variable_names"},{"category":"method","location":"#PlanetPostStats.TimeSeriesMeSd.write_field!-Tuple{PlanetPostStats.TimeSeriesMeSd.OutputFile, PlanetPostStats.TimeSeriesMeSd.TimeSeriesConfig, AbstractString, AbstractArray{<:Real}, AbstractDict, Symbol}","page":"Home","text":"write_field!(of::OutputFile, cfg, name, data, attrib, vertical::Symbol)\n\nAppends the Float32 variable name with values data to the output file of with PlanetTools.ReadWritePlanet.writenetcdf.\n\ndata must have the dimensions (lon, lat[, level or plev][, time]) of the file (singleton lon/lat for zm/gm files); vertical is :none for 2D variables, :model for model levels, and :pressure for pressure levels. Missing values (NaN) are written as missing, i.e. as cfg.fill_value, which is set as _FillValue; writenetcdf encodes them correctly. The attribute cell_methods is composed from the file's temporal method and its spatial representation, e.g. \"time: annual mean; lon: mean\"; attrib (e.g. units, long_name) is copied. The variable is compressed with cfg.deflatelevel.\n\nExample\n\nwrite_field!(of, cfg, \"prsurf\", ats_gm, OrderedDict(\"units\" => \"hPa\"), :none)\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PlanetPostStats.TimeSeriesMeSd.write_field!"},{"category":"method","location":"#PlanetPostStats.TimeSeriesMeSd.yearmonth_dates-Tuple{AbstractVector{PlanetPostStats.TimeSeriesMeSd.YearMonth}}","page":"Home","text":"yearmonth_dates(months::AbstractVector{YearMonth}) -> Vector{Dates.Date}\n\nConverts model months to Dates.Dates (first day of the month), the time axis expected by PlanetTools. Only year and month of the dates are used by PlanetTools, so the Gregorian calendar of Date does not affect results for other planets.\n\nExample\n\njulia> yearmonth_dates([YearMonth(3, 2)])\n1-element Vector{Dates.Date}:\n 0003-02-01\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PlanetPostStats.TimeSeriesMeSd.yearmonth_dates"},{"category":"method","location":"#PlanetPostStats.TimeSeriesMeSd.yearmonth_range-Tuple{PlanetPostStats.TimeSeriesMeSd.YearMonth, PlanetPostStats.TimeSeriesMeSd.YearMonth}","page":"Home","text":"yearmonth_range(first::YearMonth, last::YearMonth) -> Vector{YearMonth}\n\nAll months from first to last, both inclusive, in chronological order. Returns an empty vector if last < first.\n\nExample\n\njulia> yearmonth_range(YearMonth(1, 11), YearMonth(2, 2))\n4-element Vector{YearMonth}:\n YearMonth(1, 11)\n YearMonth(1, 12)\n YearMonth(2, 1)\n YearMonth(2, 2)\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PlanetPostStats.TimeSeriesMeSd.yearmonth_range"},{"category":"method","location":"#PlanetPostStats.TimeSeriesMeSd.yyyy-Tuple{Integer}","page":"Home","text":"yyyy(year::Integer) -> String\n\nFour-digit, zero-padded representation of a model year as used in ModelE file names and in the output file names of this package (3 → \"0003\").\n\nExample\n\njulia> yyyy(3)\n\"0003\"\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PlanetPostStats.TimeSeriesMeSd.yyyy"}]
}
